   "notes": [
    "Capital raised = ATM issuance \u2212 repurchases, common and preferred. Cash is an existing balance, never counted as a raise. The waterfall reads down: common + preferred + cash drawn (or \u2212 cash kept) = BTC + DIVs. Strive's common figure is an estimate: net share change \u00d7 prior-week VWAP.",
    "BTC = the week's bitcoin purchase cost, fees included (MSTR: SEC 8-K aggregate purchase price (data/strategy-weekly-8k.json) \u00b7 ASST: strive.com dashboard purchase cost). DIVs = the rest of the week's funding: preferred dividends and interest, plus fees and other uses. Strategy's 8-K put the week's dividends and interest at $57.4m; the difference is rounding in its $0.01B balances.",
    "Amplification uses each issuer's own formula, shown in \u00d7. Strategy: BTC reserve \u00f7 net BTC reserve (BTC + USD \u2212 debt \u2212 preferred), its strategy.com KPI since July 23, 2026. Strive: 1 + (debt + SATA notional) \u00f7 BTC value, where the ratio is the \"Amplification Ratio\" on its treasury dashboard; Strive has no debt. The two measure different things and are not comparable. Weekly changes come from the filed balances.",
    "NAV, price/NAV, coverage and growth are estimates from dated balances and reconstructed preferred claims at the displayed prices; growth holds prices constant.",
    "USD cover = months of dividend (and, for Strategy, interest) obligations held in USD, read against Strategy's 12-month floor and Strive's 18-month goal. Coverage = (BTC + cash) \u00f7 annual obligations; break-even = obligations \u00f7 BTC value. MSTR: strategy.com KPIs \u00b7 ASST: strive.com dashboard, SATA stated rate 13.0%.",
    "Multi-week growth window: MSTR since Aug 30 \u00b7 ASST since Aug 28.",
    "Avg cost = aggregate bitcoin purchase price \u00f7 BTC held, fees included; vs cost = BTC price \u00f7 avg cost \u2212 1; cost basis = the aggregate purchase price. MSTR: SEC 8-K (data/strategy-weekly-8k.json) \u00b7 ASST: strive.com dashboard cost basis."
